{
  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "91316",
      "field": "detail",
      "english": "This far from the Undercity, logistics are challenging and we have a dire shortage of building materials needed to help restore this fortress. I'd like your help with that.\n\nThe ruined village of Shadowvale can be found in the Whispering Forest, just southwest of here. One of the buildings has an old root cellar used to store all sorts of things. There are likely to be usable materials down there. Scavenge what you can and return to us."
    },
    {
      "id": "91316",
      "field": "objective",
      "english": "Collect 12 pieces of Sturdy Lumber from Shadowvale in Tirisfal Glades."
    },
    {
      "id": "91317",
      "field": "title",
      "english": "The Tarnished"
    },
    {
      "id": "91317",
      "field": "detail",
      "english": "Not all risen paladins have acclimated well to our new existence, as you may have seen yourself already. Some have carried forward their prejudices from life, and continue to visit violence upon their fellow Forsaken.\n\nAs it stands we are mistrusted by our people who remember well the persecution inflicted by the living in the name of the light, and these attacks do not help. A number of these tarnished have taken up residence at Shadowvale to the southwest. End them and bring me their leader's head."
    },
    {
      "id": "91317",
      "field": "objective",
      "english": "Slay 8 Tarnished Drudges, 6 Tarnished Zealots, and collect the head of Commander Rudolph Gelhardt in Tirisfal Glades."
    },
    {
      "id": "94427",
      "field": "title",
      "english": "A Lesson in Divinity"
    },
    {
      "id": "94427",
      "field": "detail",
      "english": "A key tenent of being a paladin is the pursuit of divinity. This is not the pursuit of godhood, but merely the pursuit of good itself, for good's sake. We've all arrived at this place due to tragedy of one form or another, and it would be easy to lose that grace that defined us as paladins in life.\n\nGo to the Undercity and seek out Tanis Alderwood in the Trade Quarter. They are in need, and they could benefit greatly from some grace."
    },
    {
      "id": "94427",
      "field": "objective",
      "english": "Speak to Tanis Alderwood in the Undercity."
    },
    {
      "id": "94434",
      "field": "title",
      "english": "A Lesson in Divinity"
    },
    {
      "id": "94434",
      "field": "detail",
      "english": "Wait, you want to... help? Why would a paladin want to help a beggar like me?\n\nWell, I suppose that you could be of some assistance. \n\nIt's my wife you see. She, well... she's falling apart. I mean that literally. The apothecaries can stitch her back together right as rain, but they are about the Dark Lady's business and none are available to help. If you could perhaps bring me some fresh cloth then I could at least make her a wrapping to hold her together while we wait for the apothecaries."
    },
    {
      "id": "94434",
      "field": "objective",
      "english": "Bring 10 Linen Cloth to Tanis Alderwood in the Undercity."
    },
    {
      "id": "94435",
      "field": "title",
      "english": "A Lesson in Divinity"
    },
    {
      "id": "94435",
      "field": "detail",
      "english": "I don't know why you'd go out of your way to help me, but I appreciate it. If someone sent you my way, tell them I appreciate them too. You'll always have a friend in Tanis Alderwood, <Class>."
    },
    {
      "id": "94435",
      "field": "objective",
      "english": "Return to Danitha Morr at Bandarion Keep."
    },
    {
      "id": "94436",
      "field": "title",
      "english": "A Lesson in Divinity"
    },
    {
      "id": "94436",
      "field": "detail",
      "english": "It's time to demonstrate your ability to channel one of the light's greatest gifts.\n\nThe item I just gave you is called the Symbol of Life. Take care, as it may cause you some discomfort to handle a talisman of the light such as this. The light may be anathema to the force that created us, but it is still our guide and ally. The pain reminds us of this.\n\nGo see Deathguard Billmuth downstairs. He just arrived and he has petitioned us for aid. Show him and the Forsaken what a true paladin can do."
    },
    {
      "id": "94436",
      "field": "objective",
      "english": "Speak with Deathguard Billmuth at Bandarion Keep.\n\nShould you misplace your Symbol of Life, return to Danitha Morr for a replacement."
    },
    {
      "id": "94436",
      "field": "complete",
      "english": "Speak with Deathguard Billmuth at Bandarion Keep."
    },
    {
      "id": "94438",
      "field": "title",
      "english": "A Lesson in Divinity"
    },
    {
      "id": "94438",
      "field": "detail",
      "english": "Falgan and I were sent on a mission to scout out scarlet activity in Venomweb Vale. We managed to sneak close enough to one of their camps to hear about new orders involving an attack on Brill. Before we could decide what to do next, I stepped on a twig and the noise alerted them to us.\n\nFalgan yelled at me to run, so I ran. By the time I realized he wasn't with me, I was halfway to Brill. That brave idiot probably stayed behind to hold them off for me.\n\nPlease, find my friend and help him if you can."
    },
    {
      "id": "94438",
      "field": "objective",
      "english": "Take the Symbol of Life and use it to resurrect Deathguard Falgan at Venomweb Vale. \n\nShould you misplace your Symbol of Life, return to Danitha Morr for a replacement."
    },
    {
      "id": "94438",
      "field": "complete",
      "english": "Take the Symbol of Life and use it to resurrect Deathguard Falgan at Venomweb Vale."
    },
    {
      "id": "94440",
      "field": "title",
      "english": "A Lesson in Divinity"
    },
    {
      "id": "94440",
      "field": "detail",
      "english": "These Scarlet Crusaders often carry satchels with their deployment orders. We know an attack is coming, but if we can recover their orders, we can warn the rest of the Deathguard and prepare an ambush. \n\nYou are clearly an impressive paladin. Kill these scarlet animals and retrieve a copy of their orders and bring them back to Deathguard Billmuth. He'll take it from there."
    },
    {
      "id": "94440",
      "field": "objective",
      "english": "Retrieve the Scarlet Crusade Attack Plans from the Scarlet Crusaders at Venomweb Vale, and return to Deathguard Billmuth at Bandarion Keep."
    },
    {
      "id": "94441",
      "field": "title",
      "english": "A Lesson in Divinity"
    }
  ],
